  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "ChalkQL 0.6 lets standing views and refreshes run side by side, rebinds a view's parameters without planning again, and maintains window functions incrementally.\n\n      - **Views and refreshes:** An update a refresh overtakes is published at the version it read, never thrown away, and no refresh waits for a view. A refresh that writes nothing a view reads moves the view on without computing. Commits carry a stamp of version and generation, and `UpdateToAsync` waits for one. `RefreshBuilder.Barrier()` marks a refresh every view publishes itself, and `ViewVersions.Every` makes a view publish every version, in order.\n      - **Rebindable parameters:** `ViewOptions.Rebindable` and `RebindAsync` move a view's parameters, lists included up to a declared capacity, keeping its plan. Maintained incrementally, only the operators that read a moved value run again.\n      - **Maintained windows (experimental):** `ROW_NUMBER`, `RANK`, `LAG`, `LEAD`, running aggregates and the like are maintained from the rows a change reaches, rather than recomputed.\n      - **Planner and execution fixes:** set operations over columns of different precisions plan; a parameter in a `CASE` branch and a window's constant parameter type; timestamps are cut to their declared precision; hash joins with many rows per key build in linear time.\n      - **Compatibility:** No public API is removed or changed. A view now sends readers a commit at a version it relabels without an update, and timestamps cast to a precision lose the digits beyond it. The wire protocol and IR version are unchanged; a 0.5 planner serves a 0.6 client but lacks the planner's fixes.\n\n      Full release notes:\n      https://github.com/markhammond/chalkql/releases/tag/v0.6",
